sentences.t:
Tum Danai gemitu atque ereptae virginis ira
undique collecti invadunt, acerrimus Aiax,
et gemini Atridae, Dolopumque exercitus omnis;

sentences.l:
Then the Danaans, by the groan and by anger at the maiden snatched away,
from every side gathered, attack, most fierce Ajax,
and the twin Atridae, and of the Dolopes the whole army;

sentences.t:
adversi rupto ceu quondam turbine venti
confligunt, Zephyrusque Notusque et laetus Eois
Eurus equis;

sentences.l:
Opposed, as when once a whirlwind having burst, the winds
clash, both Zephyr and Notus and glad with eastern
Eurus with horses;

sentences.t:
Illi etiam, si quos obscura nocte per umbram
fudimus insidiis totaque agitavimus urbe,
apparent;

sentences.l:
Those too, if any whom in the dark night through the shadow
we routed by ambush and chased through the whole city,
appear;

sentences.t:
primusque Coroebus
Penelei dextra divae armipotentis ad aram
procumbit;

sentences.l:
and first Coroebus
by Peneleus's right hand, at the altar of the war-mighty goddess,
falls forward;

sentences.t:
Divellimur inde,
Iphitus et Pelias mecum, quorum Iphitus aevo
iam gravior, Pelias et volnere tardus Ulixi;

sentences.l:
We are torn apart from there,
Iphitus and Pelias with me, of whom Iphitus by age
now heavier, and Pelias slow by a wound of Ulysses;

sentences.t:
adgressi ferro circum, qua summa labantis
iuncturas tabulata dabant, convellimus altis
sedibus, impulimusque;

sentences.l:
having attacked with iron around, where the topmost floors
gave the joints loosening, we tear it from its high
seat, and drive it on;

sentences.t:
Ipse inter primos correpta dura bipenni
limina perrumpit, postisque a cardine vellit
aeratos;

sentences.l:
He himself among the foremost, a double axe having been seized, the hard
thresholds breaks through, and from the hinge tears the doorposts
bronze-sheathed;
